# Model binaries — ARCHITECTURE_RULES.md R14.5.
# ~636 MB of ONNX graphs, SentencePiece models and vocab dictionaries. Committing these once
# puts them in history permanently; removing them later requires rewriting every downstream clone.
*.onnx
# `*.onnx` alone stopped being enough once weights moved out of the graph: dedup_weights.py
# writes the shared blob as a plain `.bin`, so a 276 MB file sat untracked and one `git add -A`
# from history. The rule is about model bytes, not about a file extension.
*.bin
*.weights
model.SRC*
model.TGT*
dict.*.json
# The acoustic models are 137 MB of binaries and stay out — but their `conf/` directories do not.
# `model.conf` is 289 bytes of decode configuration: a tuning decision, not model bytes. §3.34
# narrowed Hindi's beam there, and under the old rule that change would have lived on one laptop —
# invisible to review, absent from a fresh clone, and silently undone by whoever next staged the
# models. Excluded as contents (`/**`) rather than as a directory, because git will not re-include
# anything beneath an excluded *directory* however many `!` rules follow it.
/app/src/main/assets/model/**
!/app/src/main/assets/model/conf/
!/app/src/main/assets/model/conf/**
/app/src/main/assets/model-hi/**
!/app/src/main/assets/model-hi/conf/
!/app/src/main/assets/model-hi/conf/**

# Python virtualenvs for the ONNX export pipeline. V3.4.1 committed one, numpy headers and all.
/model_pipeline/**/venv/
/model_pipeline/**/*_env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Benchmark output — raw runs are large and machine-specific. Frozen baselines are committed
# deliberately, by path, not by accident.
/bench/results/*/raw/

# IDE session state and raw benchmark logcat dumps: local artefacts, not evidence.
# The parsed evidence lives in model_pipeline/*.jsonl and docs/.
/.idea/
/model_pipeline/*.log
